        { "@type": "Question", "name": "Does collagen get rid of cellulite?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "No. Two randomised trials have reported improvement in cellulite measures after an oral collagen supplement, but both tested specific branded peptides, one reached significance only in normal-weight women, and neither has been independently replicated. Nothing in that evidence supports removing cellulite, and no supplement should be sold as doing so." } },
        { "@type": "Question", "name": "How much collagen did the cellulite trials use?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "The 2015 trial used 2.5g a day of a branded bioactive collagen peptide for six months. The 2026 trial used 1,000mg a day of a branded low-molecular-weight collagen peptide for 24 weeks. Both doses are smaller than the 8,000mg of hydrolysed marine collagen in a Collabloom shot, which tells you that the peptide used mattered more than the quantity." } },
        { "@type": "Question", "name": "How long would I have to take it to see anything?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Longer than most people try. The two trials ran for six months and 24 weeks, and the 2026 trial reported its first significant cellulite difference at week 12. There is no evidence of any change in four or six weeks, so a short trial of a collagen shot is not a test of this question." } },
        { "@type": "Question", "name": "Do anti-cellulite creams, oils and sprays work?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Not for the dimpling. Reviews have found no cream, gel, oil, massager or dry brush shown in a properly controlled trial to reduce cellulite in any lasting way, because nothing applied to the surface reaches the fibrous septae that cause it. A 2026 fact-check of a viral Indian anti-cellulite spray advertisement concluded the claim was false." } },
        { "@type": "Question", "name": "Will losing weight get rid of my cellulite?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "It can make it less visible, but it does not remove it. Reducing the fat between the septae lowers the pressure pushing the skin up, yet the septae themselves are unchanged, which is why lean women also have cellulite. Where weight loss is large or rapid, loose skin can become the more noticeable problem." } },
        { "@type": "Question", "name": "What is the best treatment for cellulite?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "The clinic procedures with the most support are acoustic wave therapy, the 1440nm Nd:YAG minimally invasive laser and subcision, which were the modalities singled out by a 2015 review of 67 studies and a 2024 systematic review. Even these are described as promising rather than proven, with short follow-up, and the only injectable drug ever approved for cellulite stopped being manufactured in December 2022." } },
        { "@type": "Question", "name": "Is cellulite a sign that something is wrong with my health?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "No. Cellulite is thought to affect roughly 80 to 90% of women after puberty at every body size, and it reflects the orientation of the connective tissue bands under the skin rather than body fat or ill health. Painful dimpling, firm nodules, swelling that pits, sudden onset or any puckering on the breast are different and should be examined." } }
